{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 9.495,
   "text": "My first night on the hospital front desk, the old guard slid the visitor log across to me."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 10.095,
   "end": 13.977,
   "text": "After two a.m., everyone signs in. Everyone."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 14.777,
   "end": 20.196,
   "text": "And if someone signs a patient's name... instead of their own... you do not let them up."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 21.096,
   "end": 26.963,
   "text": "For three weeks, that log stayed empty. Just humming lights, and rain against the glass doors."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 27.863,
   "end": 31.276,
   "text": "Then, at two-fifteen, the doors slid open."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 32.876,
   "end": 38.764,
   "text": "An old woman shuffled in. Barefoot. Soaking wet. A hospital bracelet on her wrist."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 39.564,
   "end": 43.383,
   "text": "She signed the log without a word... and smiled at me."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 44.383,
   "end": 47.113,
   "text": "Ruth Ellery. Room four-twelve."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 48.513,
   "end": 53.292,
   "text": "I checked the screen. Ruth Ellery was upstairs. Fourth floor. Asleep."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 54.292,
   "end": 57.215,
   "text": "I'm sorry, ma'am... I can't let you up."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 58.515,
   "end": 63.208,
   "text": "Her smile went away. She turned... and walked back out into the rain."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 66.208,
   "end": 71.733,
   "text": "At three, the fourth floor called down. Ruth Ellery had passed away... in her sleep."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 73.133,
   "end": 79.64,
   "text": "At dawn, I went to close the log. Under her name, in the same shaky handwriting, was a second line."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 80.64,
   "end": 83.328,
   "text": "My name... Room four-thirteen."
  }
 ],
